# Remote @require. This file is identical to ../demo.flow except for
# one line: the @require directive. Nothing in text/library.go changes
# when the library is published — the module path is the only thing
# that differs.
#
# This file will not run until you actually publish
# text/ to a public Git repository under the path below. It is here
# as documentation of the two forms.

# @require ./text                                (local, this repo)
@require github.com/nexssp/flow/examples/m6_require/text v1.0.0

@config:verbosity=2

{ message: "hello from a published library" }
-> text_tools.uppercase
-> log.info
